  "scope": "Downed native flyer only: capture, hold, claws sweep absorption, blade absorption, claws head absorption, live release, and a last-chance save followed by a real lethal blade session. Transition frames remain unresolved; this is not full creature/mod/terrain acceptance.",
  "fixes": [
    "Shared native receiver pose and actual head/thorax surface grip",
    "Torso-sized carry clearance instead of the entire wing span",
    "Original flyer_com_idle wing fold retained instead of human arm projection; horizontal body faces its carrier",
    "Ragdoll pose history resets on a backwards client world-clock correction instead of crashing or reusing future skin snapshots",
    "Rigid blade grip uses the actual forearm-bound mesh anchor, preserving the original anchor before wrist-space conversion",
    "Native receiver facing follows the paired scene before entity yaw interpolation catches up",
    "Removed victims cannot access invalidated Forge capabilities through RagdollDrive.captured",
    "Finite hurt-flash duration survives a client world-clock rewind without extending a corpse red overlay until the old absolute deadline",
    "Consume cutting uses the same connected-joint projection and component support lift as the rendered skin, instead of independently interpolated bone positions",
    "Fit the right arm using actual sharp-profile points near the authored blade marker; preserve arm length, wrist, left arm and root",
    "One authored blade slice can be authorized by either sharp side, with independent sampled paths but a shared completion event; separate claws retain their own sections",
    "Prefer confirmed central tissue contact over a broad wing bounding volume",
    "Choose the physical root through mesh/bone ancestry, then prefer the trunk among sibling roots; broad child wings no longer invert their skeleton",
    "Evaluate all visible sharp profiles before selecting the shared blade section",
    "Use exact two-bone fitting across the actual authored slicing poses; the previous CCD candidate search failed a reachable source pose",
    "Bind both sever blood emitters to actual cap triangles and their component motion; sharp absorption no longer substitutes a timed body-center spray"
