    "boundary": "TimeBegin bytes were re-read directly. SpawnGib ownership/names use the existing reverse-engineered audit schema. Two source spawn events do not imply two full-body cutting planes or arbitrary mesh slicing."
  },
  "sourceBoundary": "Native P2 flyer idle wing-fold curves are reused on its existing MC rig. The P1 blade receiver split marker is verified at 0.833333 seconds. Horizontal-body carry orientation, human receiver retargeting, blade arm fitting and runtime mesh sections are MC adaptations, not a claim that an original flyer absorption sequence has been recovered.",
  "cutCountMeaning": "cuts counts intersected model parts split by confirmed sections; it is not the number of blade strokes or unique cutting planes.",
  "firstHoldWithinBound": true,
  "pending": [
    "Wrong wing-root ownership is fixed in these native cases; preSeverEdgeToThoraxCenter records the improved proximity. Retained real skin contacts still authorize sections, and continuous contact timing across varied receivers remains unaccepted.",
    "The bounded native blade cases cut the actual thorax into two sides without duplicate blade-side sections; arbitrary receiver shapes and final section appearance still need a broader matrix",
    "Capture/hold/consume transition continuity and skin/terrain clearance through the whole sequence",
    "High-speed thin obstacles, uneven floors and multiplayer/crowd/mod matrix",
    "Remaining creatures, audio and original-game combat acceptance; whole active goal remains incomplete"
  ],
  "measurementBoundary": "The cut-query audit compares the production connectedPose result with each same-frame rendered part position (including support lift), and reports the difference from raw interpolated physics as a diagnostic. It is not an acceptance of the receiver choreography or final topology. Receiver triangles come from native baked-mesh world matrices. A QA-only mixin records the mature weapon anchor inside BlacklightClawLayer.renderMesh using the exact draw PoseStack and blended wrist deformation; it does not re-run animation. Render-time equality and mature rigid material are asserted for every held frame. Independent post-frame pose samples remain as a diagnostic, not acceptance authority. Distances can include an anchor embedded inside the receiver surface. This does not measure liquid/growing weapons or certify every hand/receiver contact throughout consumption.",
  "validation": "Both native clients compiled and ran five scripted gameplay scenes. Successful damage, last-chance ownership, live-body integrity, actual drawn grip-to-native-triangle distances, two-sided thorax sections, one event per authored blade slice, short hurt overlays and completion were checked. Twelve focused unit suites (56 cases per platform) cover backwards-clock invalidation, finite blade/skin intersection, delayed cut generations, connected joint projection, actual sharp-profile fitting without changing arm lengths, original split timing, hierarchy-aware root choice across sparse/forest/cyclic rigs, actual skin support on slabs/steps, connected side-wall separation, finite recovery/current joint anchors and native-renderer offset settling, and finite hit flashes across clock rewinds. Prior broad server/unit regression checkpoints are not represented as rerun by this report.",
  "visualReview": {
    "status": "keyframe_sheets_reviewed",
    "sheets": 10,
    "framesPerSheet": 16,
    "boundary": "All frame metadata were checked; visual inspection covers the ten selected keyframe sheets, not a manual pixel review of every captured frame."
  }
